<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hog run estim Tuesday 105,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hog run estim Tuesday 105,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts steady to $.50 per cwt lower compared with midsession Monday.</p>
<p>Trade moderate for light to moderate demand and offerings.</p>
<p>Tuesday's estimate: 105,000  Wk ago: 93,000 Yr ago: 94,000</p>
<p>US 1-3 46-49% Carcass Base Lean* Country	     Plants</p>
<p>220-260 lbs			  55.00 -56.50    56.00 -57.50</p>
<p>	 few				    57.00	     58.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs			  54.00 -56.50    54.50 -57.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs			  54.00 -56.50    54.50 -57.50</p>
<p>Sows:  generally steady to 1.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3   300-450 lbs.	    42.00 -45.00   44.00 -47.00</p>
<p>	   450-500 lbs.	    44.00 -46.00   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>	   500 lbs. up	     46.00 -49.00   47.00 -50.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct. lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in  base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
